Grove PATCH-27: settle a bid parked in BID_ERROR whose chain-A redeem is
already confirmed

BID_ERROR is terminal for the adaptor-signature state machine
(checkXmrBidState has no branch for it), and PWNDA-PATCH-11's recovery
re-queues the chain-A redeem so a TRANSIENT failure can be retried. It has a
blind spot the 2026-08-23 mainnet swap fell into: the redeem was not merely
built, it had CONFIRMED -- the engine parked the bid on a duplicate-broadcast
rejection of a transaction that was already in a block. Re-queueing that
redeem returns early from redeemXmrBidCoinALockTx ("already redeemed"), so
the bid can only ever rest at LOCK_RELEASED, `in_progress`, for as long as
the database exists. Twelve days later it was still the console's one
"Swap in Progress" (status Error), and the wallet's tracker still said
"Waiting for the other user".

  basicswap.py  pwndaRecoverStalledBid
      New gate between "no refund in flight" and "nothing was ever built":
      when the engine's own record carries the chain-A spend txid AND chain A
      reports >= 1 confirmation for it, the swap is financially complete for
      the side that redeemed A. Settle it exactly as
      process_XMR_SWAP_A_LOCK_tx_spend does on seeing the spend -- SCRIPT_TX_
      REDEEMED, LOCK_TX_A_SPEND_TX_SEEN event, then SWAP_COMPLETED for the
      redeeming side -- and deactivate it so it leaves the in-progress set.
      The other side (was_received) completes on chain B and is NOT settled
      here; the reply says so. Reply gains `settled: true`, `confirmations`
      and `txid` so a caller can tell "settled" from "re-queued".

  basicswap.py  pwndaTxConfirmations
      Confirmations for a chain-A transaction: the electrum backend's verbose
      lookup, or getrawtransaction then the wallet's gettransaction. None
      means "unknown", and unknown never settles.

Idempotent and refusal-shaped like PATCH-11: it changes no state unless the
chain has already made the outcome a fact. The supervisor's bid janitor
(Rust, swap_bid.rs) calls this for every "Error" row on sentbids after each
healthy start and periodically, which is what turns the 2026-08-23 bid into
"Completed" without anyone finding a button.

Not an upstream candidate as written: upstream's exit is manualBidUpdate on
the HTML bid page, which takes an arbitrary state. This takes none.

diff --git a/basicswap/basicswap.py b/basicswap/basicswap.py
--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
